WEBVTT

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:32.040
You don't think something's happened to Joe, do you?

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.820
It's been three days now.

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:51.650
Hey, old man, you think we should report him missing to the police?

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.400
No. He'll be back.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:58.280
Okay.{remove?}

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.410
He... He...

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:06.910
Old man?

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:12.460
He'll be back! He has to come back!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.080
As long as he still has boxing, he'll come back!

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.290
Come in.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.810
You're still not ready yet? You'll be late.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:41.230
All right.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:55.520
Today's in-ring memorial will be our last farewell to Rikiishi-kun.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.740
Stop! Break!

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.790
Fight!

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.170
Stop! Break!

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:19.880
What the hell are you doing?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.880
<i>You only have a round left!</i>

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.150
Stop!

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.340
Get back! That's the bell!

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.520
The final round's over!

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.530
Stop! Didn't you hear the bell?

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:29.470
What, done already?

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:31.810
Udagawa!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.650
<i>Now, before we move on to the main event,</i>

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:56.790
<i>we would like to honor the death of the late Rikiishi Toru,</i>

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:01.680
<i>and hold a ten-count bell in his memory.</i>

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.300
<i>All officials, please rise.</i>

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:10.780
What're they doing?

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:12.750
They said it's a ten-something bell.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:17.010
They're gonna ring the bell ten times in Rikiishi's memory.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:18.310
Oh?

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:59.320
Rikiishi Toru, huh?

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.070
Yeah, I heard he died.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:04.780
Hey, we'd better stand up.

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:07.190
You're right. He's dead, after all.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:11.120
Hey, stand up!

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:12.160
Sure.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:49.490
<i>Thank you very much! Now, we will continue with our main event!</i>

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:53.160
<i>In the red corner, the Oriental Junior Lightweight Champion...</i>

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.530
<i>Kageyama Mitsuo!</i>

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:56.020
Now that's what we've been waiting for!

00:07:56.020 --> 00:08:00.230
We want an uppercut! Take him down with an uppercut!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.540
Make this quick, for once!

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.510
Yeah! Go in for the kill!

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.510
Yeah! You're doing good!

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:17.200
Yeah! That's it! Get him!

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:27.090
The audience has already forgotten about Rikiishi-kun.

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:30.360
Yes. And the ring...

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:36.200
is seeking yet another blood sacrifice.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.850
That's how the world of boxing is, Yohko.

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:46.940
Yohko. Let's go home.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:50.300
Oh. Yes.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:12.610
We won't come here ever again.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.490
Grandfather, you're planning...

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.510
to dissolve Shiraki Gym, aren't you?

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:45.690
I only started Shiraki Gym because of Rikiishi Toru in the first place.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:50.520
What meaning is there in keeping the gym open without him?

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:59.380
Please, stop the car.

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:01.550
Stop the car.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.990
I'll get off here.

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:08.340
Yohko?

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:11.590
I want to think alone.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.370
You go home ahead of me, Grandfather.

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:19.230
The curtain's already been closed, Yohko.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.050
Don't overthink it.

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.590
I know.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.300
Hey, watch it!

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.800
Come on, don't make a scene.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.260
Get it together, now.{added}

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:58.380
What's the problem with kids these days?

00:10:58.380 --> 00:10:59.470
Now, now.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:33.820
Hey, stop! Stop the car!

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.370
That's definitely Yabuki.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:47.680
He looks like a ghost, but that's Yabuki, all right.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:54.440
Now this'll make a great scoop. The boxer who beat his opponent to death...

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:57.460
...Has hit rock bottom. We need to capture that!

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:01.000
We could make a documentary on him!

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.700
Hey, where are your eyes at?

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.960
Listen! Watch where you're going! Got it?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.140
Come on, take more pictures.

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.010
I got it!

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:35.090
Hey, handsome! A little early to go home, isn't it?

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:37.190
No, no, we're good.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:39.690
Oh, no!

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:41.210
Skinflints!

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.950
Here! He turned this way!

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:00.910
Well, if it isn't Yabuki-kun himself.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:02.840
I-I can't believe we're seeing you here!

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:06.620
This is a complete coincidence...

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:16.920
U-Uh, well, you see, we're...

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:21.300
We're sorry. Just hold on.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:25.490
We're, uh... sorry for getting too carried away with our work!

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:31.200
Hey, what are you waiting for? Get out the film already!

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:32.300
R-Right!{added}

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:37.920
This should be enough, right?

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:42.550
We're sorry for secretly taking pictures of you.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.590
Yeah, we're real sorry.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:47.690
I don't give a damn about the film.

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:52.560
You mind lending me some money?

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:54.380
Money?

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:59.060
Just a little. I'll pay it back later.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.530
Wh-What'll you use it for?

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:08.020
Screw it.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.560
Wait! We'll lend you whatever you need!

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.790
Here! This should be enough!

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:16.760
Thanks.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:23.210
Yabuki-kun, I'm guessing you're using that money to go drinking, right?

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:33.150
So that's it. You're trying to escape the cruelty of reality.

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:37.300
You want to use alcohol to make you forget about Rikiishi's death!

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:46.740
I see now! You should've said so earlier!

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:51.240
I mean, it's not like I could lecture you about the evils of alcohol as you are now.

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:55.030
But if you drink around here, you'll only get more and more miserable.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:58.310
We can show you somewhere, if you like.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:14:59.460
Right, guys?

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:06.420
All right, then it's a deal!

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:10.730
We can show you a bar that's cheery, if a bit noisy.

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:13.520
After all, we've been bothering you with our reporting!

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:15.390
We've got to make it up to you!

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:22.670
Hey, take us to the Baron.

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:24.390
Huh? But that's...

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:27.400
It's fine. He needs a lively bar like that.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.400
But are you sure about this?

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:50.880
What do you think about this place, Yabuki-kun?

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:24.460
Hey, did you bring Yabuki here because you knew Shiraki Yohko comes here?

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:26.270
Do you want headlines or not?

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:35.700
A boxer who's become a wooden puppet from the shock of killing his opponent

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:39.150
meets the granddaughter of a gym's president,

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:41.830
who's out dancing to forget her protégé boxer's death.{3 liner - split by editor}

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.500
This has all the makings of a great story.

00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:55.400
I never thought I'd see you here.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.130
What're you doing?

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:00.190
Didn't you see? I was dancing.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.890
And what did you come here for?

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.100
To drink.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.610
Hey! Yohko!

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:20.380
Well, haven't you made your way up in the world?

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:23.160
The hungry boy who could barely find anything to eat,

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:28.930
and only knew how to swing his gloves in the square jungle,

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:33.910
now has money to waste on drink and play!

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:35.670
Now, aren't you just great?

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:40.260
It must be hard to stand.

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:42.180
Why don't you have a seat?

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:53.940
I thought you had a little bit more heart.

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:58.900
I thought you had a little more backbone. But I misjudged you.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.910
Hey, who's that bum talking to Yohko?

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:08.740
Hey, that's Yabuki!

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:09.750
Yabuki?

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.920
Yeah, the boxer that killed Rikiishi!

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:21.930
I once saw you lying on the ground at Tamahime Park, the one near Tange Gym.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:28.030
It was a snowy night, if I remember right.

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:31.440
And you've been lying down ever since.

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:36.260
You must have given up on bringing yourself back up.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.950
I guess this means Rikiishi-kun died a stupid death.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:48.500
He went through an excruciating diet

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:51.950
that far exceeded his physical limits just to fight such a pathetic man,

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.710
and he ended up dying for it.

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:05.390
You dumb broad! I don't remember you earning the right to talk so high-and-mighty!

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:09.990
Listen! You don't understand anything!

00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:11.990
You don't even know what a punch feels like!

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:15.440
So cut out that retarded talk about Rikiishi dying a stupid death!

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:20.440
And speak for yourself! What's with the pale face? Tired out from all this partying?

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:22.800
You should... You should...

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.900
You should... You should...

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:28.570
You should just go die in a ditch somewhere!

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.200
Joe?

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:35.830
Joe!

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:46.970
Yabuki-kun!

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:50.470
Wait!

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:55.230
I don't mean to excuse my own actions...{original TL: "I don't mean to blow my own horn..."}

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:59.930
But I'm a woman and you're a man!

00:20:59.930 --> 00:21:03.490
Why don't you stop being a baby and man up?

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.490
And when was I a baby?

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:15.000
I'll be frank. You broke Wolf Kanagushi's jaw in the ring, and he never recovered.

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:19.460
And you even drove Rikiishi Toru to his death. You're a criminal boxer.

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:24.840
You shouldn't be happy-go-lucky enough to drink and moan here!

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:32.680
You can't do your duty as a man like this, can you?

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.510
You're in debt to them both.

00:21:34.510 --> 00:21:36.470
A sacred liability.

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:39.110
And you need to realize that right now!

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:40.310
Right now!

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:48.780
You should die in the ring, for both of them!

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:57.330
You seem to want to give up the ring, but I won't let you do that!

00:21:57.860 --> 00:21:59.890
Not even Wolf-kun would stand for that.

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:02.270
And certainly not Rikiishi-kun.

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:14.700
I'm not seeking anyone's forgiveness.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:16.580
I'll deal with my own problems myself.

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:17.800
Or are you saying

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:23.560
that someone gave <i>you</i> permission to go playing around like that?{changed for drama}

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:36.460
Y-Yohko...

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:55.630
No, Yabuki. I'm an adult.

00:22:55.630 --> 00:22:58.020
I take responsibility for what I've done.

00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:24.530
Yuke kouya wo

00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:24.530
Go to the wilderness!

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:28.370
Oira boxer

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:28.370
I am a boxer.

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:36.130
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:36.130
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:41.800
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:41.800
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:43.840
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:43.840
Howling at the moon alone.

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:50.490
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:50.490
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.490
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.490
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:57.690
Yuke kouya wo

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:57.690
Go to the wilderness!

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:01.400
Oira boxer

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:01.400
I am a boxer.

00:24:02.530 --> 00:24:09.660
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:24:02.530 --> 00:24:09.660
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!

00:24:15.640 --> 00:24:19.510
Joe's despair over losing Rikiishi is deep.

00:24:20.230 --> 00:24:23.160
Joe wanders the city at night, aimless and alone.

00:24:24.020 --> 00:24:25.890
And in the shopping district, where the neon lights flicker,

00:24:27.130 --> 00:24:30.430
Joe meets Wolf Kanagushi, who's become a yakuza bodyguard.

00:24:31.110 --> 00:24:35.110
Wolf Kanagushi, whose match with Joe was hailed as the greatest six-round match in history,

00:24:35.110 --> 00:24:39.840
who was said to be a contender for the world championship.

00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:43.120
Now, Joe's competitive spirit burns

00:24:43.640 --> 00:24:45.410
from seeing Wolf's miserable backside.{wut}

00:24:46.340 --> 00:24:47.630
"I don't want to become like Wolf."

00:24:48.710 --> 00:24:50.280
"I'm not like Wolf."

00:24:50.890 --> 00:24:52.280
"I am Yabuki Joe!"

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:55.130
Joe revives his fighting self.

00:24:56.480 --> 00:24:57.950
Joe's eyes shine!

00:24:58.550 --> 00:25:00.490
His wild eyes shine!

00:25:00.490 --> 00:25:04.920
Now, as Joe burns with fighting spirit as he looks up into the starry sky,

00:25:04.920 --> 00:25:06.540
which way is tomorrow!?
